# Source for requirements-archive.txt (regenerate with:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes -o requirements-archive.txt \
#     requirements-archive.in
# ).
#
# Dependencies for the asset-archive workflow lane
# (.github/workflows/poll-pursue.yml + verify-assets-daily.yml).
# Kept separate from requirements-poll.in because the poll lane
# itself is lean (curl_cffi + small structlog deps) and runs every
# 30 min; the archive lane only runs on detected change or daily
# verify, so installing boto3 + transitive deps there is fine.
#
# Why hash-pinning matters here specifically (laverna SEC-001):
# this lane runs with R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID + R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY in
# its env. A PyPI compromise or index-confusion attack on boto3 or
# any of its transitive deps would execute arbitrary code with R2
# bucket write access. The poll lane already enforces
# --require-hashes; this file extends that discipline to the
# archive lane.
boto3>=1.35,<2
